      "id": "mxvinme",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Keyboard"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Keyboards are the primary input devices containing alphanumeric, numeric, control, and 12 function keys (F1 to F12).",
        "Computer mice are categorized into mechanical, optical, and wireless types based on movement detection technology.",
        "Scanners convert physical hard-copy documents into digital format, with main types being flatbed, handheld, and sheetfed.",
        "Specialized optical input devices include OMR for detecting pencil marks, OCR for converting printed text to editable data, and MICR for reading magnetic ink on bank cheques."
      ],
      "id": "skfqos6"
    },
