    {
      "id": "xz6w25a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.5 OMR, OCR, MICR"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "MICR uses a 9-digit code printed with magnetic ink: the first 3 digits denote the city, middle 3 denote the bank, and last 3 denote the branch.",
        "OMR (Optical Mark Recognition) is specifically used for evaluating objective-type OMR answer sheets in competitive exams.",
        "Function key F2 is used to rename a selected file or folder, while F5 refreshes the current window."
      ],
      "id": "q5dfnib"
